insert into public.chapters (series_id, season_number, week, day, script, meta) values
('dark-moon', 1, 2, 1, $json${"week":2,"day":1,"title":"The second name","heading":"Three more names","question":"three more names on the wall. Which child is next, and can we get there first?","steps":[{"t":"say","text":"The mine is quiet again. The hoofbeats are long gone, and only the river is left, loud in the drowned mouth below. Garrick's count is still hanging in the dark.\n\n*Three more.*"},{"t":"act","label":"ASK HIM WHAT HE KNOWS"},{"t":"say","text":"He is wiping the soot from a lamp glass with the corner of his cloth, and he doesn't look up.\n\n*\"I can tell you where the next name on that wall lives. That's where I'd start.\"*"},{"t":"say","text":"At first light you find a carter bound for Fenmark who will take Tamsin home. She is still humming.\n\nShe will not get up onto the wagon. She stands in the road with her bandaged hand held against her chest, looking from one of you to the next. She settles on you."},{"t":"choice","id":0,"labels":["CROUCH DOWN TO HER","ASK WHAT THE SONG IS","SAY NOTHING. WAIT."],"mode":"flavor","branches":[]},{"t":"say","text":"*\"I wasn't asleep,\"* she says. *\"I was counting.\"*\n\n*\"One of them said, 'The mill boy next.' And the other one said to hush.\"*\n\nThen she lets the carter lift her up. She does not look back, and she does not stop humming. You can hear the counting song a long way down the road, thinner and thinner, until the wheels have it."},{"t":"say","text":"The second name scratched on that wall is **Corin**.\n\nAnd in Meira's notes, in the shorthand only Garrick has been able to place, there is a line he puts his finger on: a family at a working mill, two days south-east."},{"t":"say","text":"The Widow's Tooth is a day and a half behind you. Garrick agreed to come that far, and no further. He is shouldering a pack."},{"t":"act","label":"POINT THAT OUT"},{"t":"say","text":"He settles the strap on his shoulder. *\"Worst guests I've ever had. Good tippers, though.\"*\n\nThen he sets off down the road ahead of you, as if it had been his idea."},{"t":"say","text":"Two days down the mill road, through country that gets emptier the further you go. First the farms thin out, then the fences. By the second afternoon there is only sheep-bitten grass, and a wind off the hills that never quite drops.\n\nAt evening you come to the last farmhouse before the mill. An old man is splitting wood in the yard. He does not stop when he sees you coming. He only shifts his grip on the axe."},{"t":"notice","lines":{"Might":{"first":"He is splitting wood he does not need. The stack behind him would see out two winters.","second":"He wants that axe in his hand."},"Agility":{"first":"There are fresh ruts in the lane, and he has not once looked at them.","second":"He knows whose they are."},"Intellect":{"first":"A man afraid of strangers goes indoors. He has stayed where he can see the lane.","second":"It is not you he is watching for."},"Charm":{"first":"There is a child's face at the window, and a hand that pulls it back.","second":"He has somebody to be careful for."},"Craft":{"first":"The door-frame is older than the house: a beam from something that stood here first.","second":"Somebody built round it on purpose."},"Aim":{"first":"From his chopping-block he can see a long way up the lane toward the mill.","second":"He chose where to stand."}}},{"t":"challenge","title":"THE MAN WITH THE AXE","desc":"He saw something on this road, and he has decided not to have seen it.","options":[{"attr":"Charm","verb":"get him talking"},{"attr":"Aim","verb":"watch where his eyes keep going, and look there first"}],"reward":"+500g","fail":"he tells you to be on your way, and means it"},{"t":"say","text":"He looks at you a long while over the axe. Then he sets it down, blade into the block, and waves you to the bench by his door. The wood of it is worn pale by years of sitting.","cond":{"on":"challenge","pass":true}},{"t":"say","text":"He tells you to be on your way, and means it. It is Garrick who gets him talking in the end. He leans on the gate and offers a plain word about the weather, then the price of flour: the one subject no farmer can resist. By then the light has gone, and the old man says what he must and not a word over.","cond":{"on":"challenge","pass":false}},{"t":"say","text":"It comes out a piece at a time.\n\n*\"Three nights back. A cart went up the lane to the mill after dark. No lamps. No voices. Moving like they'd done it before.\"*\n\n*\"Before dawn it came back down the same way, and turned upriver.\"*\n\n*\"I've lived on this road sixty years. Nobody honest drives it in the dark.\"*"},{"t":"say","text":"And one thing more, which you did not have to ask for.\n\n*\"One wheel on it was dragging. I'd know that cart again by the sound alone.\"*","cond":{"on":"challenge","pass":true}},{"t":"say","text":"*No lamps. Moving like they'd done it before.*\n\nThe boy at Fenmark said that, in nearly those words, a week ago and a whole county away.\n\nThe same people."},{"t":"say","text":"You are too late to stop it. But you know which way it turned."},{"t":"say","text":"The beam over his door is older than the house. There is a loose board in it, where he swears nobody has looked in his lifetime."},{"t":"act","label":"PRISE THE BOARD"},{"t":"say","text":"Behind it: something thin, and colder than the iron nails beside it.\n\nThe old man watches you take it out. He does not ask what it is.\n\n**A locked Seeker Fragment has been added to your Chest.**","fragment":true},{"t":"say","text":"He lets you sleep in his barn. It smells of hay and old apples, and the wind finds every gap in the boards. Garrick pours the old man's cider into one more cup than there are of you, and sets it on an upturned crate at the empty place."},{"t":"say","text":"**The mill is an hour on. At first light: what did the family see?**","pull":true},{"t":"summary","lines":["**THE MILL ROAD** · Day 1","You earned: `[gold]` · Charm or Aim `[growth]`","You learned: the next name is **Corin**, the miller's boy. A cart with no lamps went up to the mill three nights ago and came back before dawn. It turned upriver. The same people who took Tamsin.","*On a failure:* You missed something on the mill road. Someone at the fire may have seen it.","Fragment: 1 found, locked","Tomorrow: **the mill, at first light**"]}]}$json$::jsonb, $json${"dc":7,"wDef":23,"wAtk":16,"fightReward":0}$json$::jsonb),
('dark-moon', 1, 2, 2, $json${"week":2,"day":2,"title":"The mill","heading":"The mill","question":"what happened at the mill?","steps":[{"t":"say","text":"The mill sits an hour on, in a fold of the valley where the stream has been made to work. You hear it before you see it: the slow knock and splash of the wheel.\n\nThe wheel is turning. That is almost worse than if it were not.\n\nNobody comes out to meet you. Three things in the yard might speak before anybody does."},{"t":"choice","id":0,"labels":["THE LATCH","THE LANE","THE WHEEL'S FOOTING"],"mode":"auto","branches":[{"options":[0],"text":"It hangs by one nail. It was broken from outside, with a single push, by somebody who did not need to try twice."},{"options":[1],"text":"Ruts in, and ruts out, four nights old. One cart. It did not turn round in the yard. Somebody led the horse about by its head, so as not to make a sound."},{"options":[2],"text":"The stone under the wheel-housing is far older than the mill built on it. Worn almost smooth into its face is a shape you know: the one on the burned rubbing. The one at the Widow's Tooth."}]},{"t":"say","text":"{F1} is still crouched in the lane. {F2} has the rubbing held flat against the footing, and is not moving."},{"t":"say","text":"A woman is standing in the mill door. She has been watching you since you came into the yard. There is flour worked deep into the creases of her hands: old flour, from before."},{"t":"notice","lines":{"Might":{"first":"The grain sacks are stacked two high where they were three.","second":"Nobody here has had the heart to lift."},"Agility":{"first":"She is standing where she can reach the door-bar without looking.","second":"She has practised that."},"Intellect":{"first":"The table behind her is laid for three.","second":"She has not been able to stop."},"Charm":{"first":"She looks at your hands before she looks at your faces.","second":"She is making sure you are not them."},"Craft":{"first":"The wheel is turning, and there is nothing in the hopper.","second":"She keeps it running so that the house will not be quiet."},"Aim":{"first":"From that doorway you can see the whole length of the lane.","second":"She watched the cart go."}}},{"t":"challenge","title":"THE MILLER'S WIFE","desc":"She will not say a word until she is sure of you, and she has no reason to be.","options":[{"attr":"Charm","verb":"get the rest of it gently"},{"attr":"Intellect","verb":"notice what she is not saying, and ask for exactly that"}],"reward":"+500g","fail":"she stops talking, and it costs you the morning"},{"t":"say","text":"When she speaks at last, it is to the yard, not to you.\n\n*\"My boy. Four nights gone. Big man, quiet, didn't even bother hiding his face — like he didn't care who saw.\"*"},{"t":"say","text":"She tells you the rest at once, as if it had been waiting behind her teeth.","cond":{"on":"challenge","pass":true}},{"t":"say","text":"And there she stops. It takes the rest of the morning to earn it back. {F3} mends the latch, and nobody asks her anything at all. The sun is high before she says it, from the doorway, and she does not ask you in.","cond":{"on":"challenge","pass":false}},{"t":"say","text":"*\"He asked for my boy by name. And he knew the night he was born — knew it better than I did.\"*"},{"t":"say","text":"Then she opens her hand. In it is a horn button, with a twist of dark thread still through it.\n\n*\"My boy got hold of his sleeve,\"* she says. *\"The man never even looked down.\"*","cond":{"on":"challenge","pass":true}},{"t":"say","text":"At the doorway, without a word, she presses a horn button into your hand, with a twist of dark thread still through it.","cond":{"on":"challenge","pass":false}},{"t":"say","text":"Behind her the wheel goes round, and round, grinding nothing.\n\nThey are not taking children.\n\nThey are collecting particular ones."},{"t":"press","title":"THE RUTS","detail":"walk the lane, and read the cart itself","harder":4,"reward":"+200g, and one more detail"},{"t":"say","text":"The left wheel pulls. You have seen that track before, coming down a muddy bank to a ford.\n\nIt is the same cart.","cond":{"on":"press"}},{"t":"say","text":"In the wheel-housing, above the footing, where years of spray should have worn anything away:"},{"t":"act","label":"REACH IN"},{"t":"say","text":"Thin, and dense, and cold in a way that running water should long since have taken out of it.\n\n**A locked Seeker Fragment has been added to your Chest.**","fragment":true},{"t":"say","text":"Garrick has said nothing all morning. On the way out he stops by the grain sacks, lifts one back up onto the stack where it used to be, and follows you down the lane.\n\nUpriver, the sky over the hills has thickened and come down low. The wind is getting up in the willows."},{"t":"say","text":"**Upriver. The ruts are four nights old, and there is weather coming.**","pull":true},{"t":"summary","lines":["**THE MILL** · Day 2","You earned: `[gold]` · Charm or Intellect `[growth]`","You learned: **Corin was asked for by name, and by the night he was born.** A big, quiet man took him four nights ago and did not hide his face. The mark from the rubbing is cut into the mill's footing.","Fragments: 2 found","Tomorrow: **upriver, on the cart's tracks**"]}]}$json$::jsonb, $json${"dc":7,"wDef":23,"wAtk":16,"fightReward":0}$json$::jsonb),
('dark-moon', 1, 2, 3, $json${"week":2,"day":3,"title":"Upriver","heading":"Upriver","question":"where did the cart go?","steps":[{"t":"say","text":"The rain came in the night. By morning the ruts are running with water, and you follow them upriver at a pace that leaves no breath for talk.\n\nThe river has risen in the dark. It runs fat and loud beside you, and the rain still comes in fits off the hills, cold on the back of the neck.\n\nThe tracks hold until the riverbank turns to stone. Then they stop.\n\nThere is no ford here. There is no reason for a cart to have come this far."},{"t":"notice","lines":{"Might":{"first":"The thorn on the left has been cut back and tied, not broken.","second":"Somebody tends it."},"Agility":{"first":"No bird is singing on the slope above.","second":"Something up there has kept them off for days."},"Intellect":{"first":"A cart does not vanish. It was unloaded here, or it went up.","second":"There is nowhere to unload."},"Charm":{"first":"In the one patch of mud, a child's shoe-print, pointing uphill.","second":"He walked this part."},"Craft":{"first":"The left wheel pulled.","second":"It left the bank at the grey slab."},"Aim":{"first":"High on the slope there is a line where the bracken lies the wrong way.","second":"A path, seen from the side."}}},{"t":"challenge","title":"WHERE THE TRACKS STOP","desc":"Somebody has been keeping a way open here without keeping it in sight.","options":[{"attr":"Craft","verb":"read the cart's own marks, and find where it left the bank"},{"attr":"Agility","verb":"slip through the thorn, by its gaps, across what looks like an old path"}],"reward":"+500g","fail":"you find the path by walking up it, in plain view and making a great deal of noise"},{"t":"say","text":"You find it from above. You come down onto the path through the wet bracken, quietly, with the whole length of it laid out below you.","cond":{"on":"challenge","pass":true}},{"t":"say","text":"It costs the afternoon. You come out onto the path at the bottom of it, scratched and filthy and cursing, and go up it the way the cart did.","cond":{"on":"challenge","pass":false}},{"t":"say","text":"Where the path narrows between two rocks, there is a dog.\n\nIt is the size of a calf. Its chain is long enough to reach both walls. The staple the chain hangs from is bright new iron, as new as the ruts.\n\nIt does not bark. It has been taught not to. It only stands up, and watches you come."},{"t":"fight","name":"THE DOG ON THE CHAIN","desc":"There is no way round it.","firstLines":["You came from above: you strike first.","It heard you on the path: it strikes first."],"strikeFirst":{"on":"challenge"}},{"t":"say","text":"Its breath smokes in the wet air. It backs away to the end of its chain and lies down with its sides heaving, and lets you by. Its eyes follow you all the way past.","cond":{"on":"fight","won":true}},{"t":"say","text":"It has you down, and it does not let go until {F1} and {F3} drag you through by the collar. Then it walks back to the middle of the path, and lies down across it again.\n\nYour sleeve is in rags. Your arm will remember its teeth for days.","cond":{"on":"fight","won":false}},{"t":"say","text":"Beyond the dog, a man is lying on the path.\n\nNot the boy. A stranger, dead a week. Whoever keeps this path has been stepping over him.\n\nGarrick crouches beside him and turns the dead man's collar up over his face. It is the first kindness anybody has done him in a week.\n\nThe dead man has a crude lockpick in one hand. It is still jammed into a small stone housing, built into the hillside itself."},{"t":"say","text":"It is old work, far older than the path, as old as the places your fragments have lain. And it is sealed.\n\nIt would not open for him."},{"t":"act","label":"SET YOUR HAND TO IT"},{"t":"say","text":"It gives at once, as if it had been waiting. The air inside is dry and still, and has not moved in a long time. What lies in it is cold.\n\n**A locked Seeker Fragment has been added to your Chest.**","fragment":true},{"t":"say","text":"A pebble skitters down the slope above you.\n\nWhen you look up there is nothing there: only a branch, still swinging, and no wind."},{"t":"say","text":"**Where was he trying to get to? The path goes on past him, and up.**","pull":true},{"t":"summary","lines":["**UPRIVER** · Day 3","You earned: `[gold]` · Craft or Agility `[growth]`","You learned: the cart went onto **a hidden path into the hillside**, kept clear and guarded. A stranger died here trying to open an old stone lock, as old as the places your fragments lay. **It opened for you.**","Fragments: 3 found","Tomorrow: **further up, to wherever the path ends**"]}]}$json$::jsonb, $json${"dc":7,"wDef":23,"wAtk":16,"fightReward":0}$json$::jsonb),
('dark-moon', 1, 2, 4, $json${"week":2,"day":4,"title":"What the hillside hides","heading":"The end of the path","question":"what is at the end of the hidden path?","steps":[{"t":"say","text":"The path climbs for an hour through bracken and scree. Up here the wind has an edge to it, and it brings you lamp-smoke before it brings you anything else.\n\nThe path ends at a hole in the hill.\n\nIt is a shaft, squared off with timber, with a ladder going down into lamplight. There are voices at the bottom."},{"t":"notice","lines":{"Might":{"first":"The ladder is new ash, pegged, and strong enough for men carrying a load.","second":"They mean to use this place for a long time."},"Agility":{"first":"The third rung from the top is worn pale on the left.","second":"Everyone who climbs this steps in the same place."},"Intellect":{"first":"Lamp-smoke, coming up steadily, and no cooking in it.","second":"Nobody lives down there. They work there."},"Charm":{"first":"The voices are not arguing, and they are not laughing.","second":"They are saying the same thing, together."},"Craft":{"first":"The shaft is old. The timbering is this year's.","second":"Somebody found it, and opened it again."},"Aim":{"first":"Straight down: a lamp, a patch of floor, and the edge of something that is not floor.","second":"A foot. Small, and bare."}}},{"t":"challenge","title":"DOWN THE SHAFT","desc":"One ladder. Whatever is down there, you will see it for as long as you are not seen.","options":[{"attr":"Agility","verb":"go down without a sound"},{"attr":"Charm","verb":"go down as if you belong, past the one posted at its foot"}],"reward":"+500g","fail":"you are seen from the top, and you see almost nothing"},{"t":"say","text":"You are halfway down before anyone looks up, and for the length of three breaths you see all of it. The air coming up past you is warm, and smells of tallow and wet stone.\n\nA chamber cut into the hill. A ring of lamps set on the floor. Hooded figures, more of them than there are of you, moving round the ring without hurry, setting things in their places.\n\nAnd in the middle, on his back on the stone, a boy. His wrists are tied. His hands lie open, palms up, and there is not a mark on them.","cond":{"on":"challenge","pass":true}},{"t":"say","text":"A lamp swings up the shaft while you are still at the top, and a watchman's eyes meet yours.\n\nBehind him: lamplight, and hooded shapes, and nothing you could swear to. But under the voices there is another sound. A boy, crying, very quietly.","cond":{"on":"challenge","pass":false}},{"t":"say","text":"He is alive."},{"t":"say","text":"Then a shout, and every hooded head below turns.\n\nThere is one ladder. One of you at a time, into their knives.\n\nYou are driven back from the shaft, into the dark. Below you, somebody hauls the ladder away. A second lamp is lit at the foot of the shaft.\n\nThey know you are here now."},{"t":"say","text":"Garrick is the last to reach you. He sits down in the roots, breathing hard. *\"That went about as well as it looked.\"*\n\nSomebody laughs, once, before they can stop it. It is the first laugh anyone has had in days."},{"t":"say","text":"You are all flat among the roots at the shaft's mouth, getting your breath back, when your hand finds something in the dark."},{"t":"act","label":"CLOSE YOUR FINGERS ON IT"},{"t":"say","text":"Rimed with frost, in the dark.\n\n**A locked Seeker Fragment has been added to your Chest.**","fragment":true},{"t":"say","text":"**Is there another way into this hill, before they finish? You have tonight to find it.**","pull":true},{"t":"summary","lines":["**THE SHAFT** · Day 4","You earned: `[gold]` · Agility or Charm `[growth]`","You learned: **Corin is alive.** He is held in a chamber cut into the hill, in a ring of lamps, by hooded figures who are making something ready. They know you are outside.","*On a pass:* there are more of them than of you, and his hands are not yet cut. There is still time.","*On a failure:* You missed something at the shaft. Someone at the fire may have seen it.","Fragments: 4 found","Tomorrow: **the hillside, tonight**"]}]}$json$::jsonb, $json${"dc":7,"wDef":23,"wAtk":16,"fightReward":0}$json$::jsonb),
('dark-moon', 1, 2, 5, $json${"week":2,"day":5,"title":"The hillside by night","heading":"The hillside, after dark","question":"who are these people, and what are they making ready?","steps":[{"t":"say","text":"Dark comes up out of the valley and over the hill. Far below, at the foot of the shaft, their lamp burns on.\n\nThere is a night to get through, and two ways to spend it."},{"t":"choice","id":0,"labels":["WALK THE HILL","READ MEIRA'S PAGES"],"mode":"auto","branches":[{"options":[0],"text":"You quarter it until your legs give out. Bracken. Scree. A sheepfold, fallen in. There is no second door."},{"options":[1],"text":"By the last of the light, in a margin, pressed hard into the paper:\n\n*\"Not one of these fragments names him. Neither does anything else I can find — every record of him scraped clean. Whoever he was, someone wanted him forgotten.\"*"}]},{"t":"say","text":"{F1} comes back off the hill with a shake of the head. {F3} is holding a page under the lamp with one finger on the margin."},{"t":"say","text":"No fragment has ever given him a name. Where they speak of him at all, they say only *him*."},{"t":"say","text":"Supper is whatever is left: hard bread, and the end of the farmer's cheese. Garrick's share ends up on somebody else's plate. He does not say where it went."},{"t":"notice","lines":{"Might":{"first":"In one place the ground rings hollow when you stamp.","second":"Not a door. A roof."},"Agility":{"first":"Something is moving on this hill that is not one of you.","second":"It knows the ground better than you do."},"Intellect":{"first":"They took their ladder away.","second":"Then they have another way out, or they do not mean to leave."},"Charm":{"first":"Nobody has said the boy's name since the shaft.","second":"Everybody is thinking it."},"Craft":{"first":"The stones of the sheepfold were cut once, and cut well.","second":"This hill was built on before it was grazed."},"Aim":{"first":"Down at the shaft: two lamps now, where there was one.","second":"They have set a watch on you."}}},{"t":"say","text":"A hooded figure comes up over the shoulder of the hill, alone, walking the way a man walks his own yard."},{"t":"fight","name":"THE ONE SENT UP TO LOOK","desc":"He has not come to talk.","firstLines":["You were walking the hill: you see him first.","You were at the lamp, reading: he sees you first."],"strikeFirst":{"on":"choice","choice":0,"options":[0]}},{"t":"say","text":"He does not say a word. He does not make a sound when he is hit. He tears himself free and is gone downhill, and what is left in your fist is a strip of his coat.\n\nSewn to it, no bigger than a thumbnail: a circle of black cloth.\n\nAt the cuff, a snapped end of dark thread, the same twist as the thread still through the horn button from the mill."},{"t":"say","text":"You hit him hard enough to wind him, and still he made no sound. You heard his teeth come together on it.","cond":{"on":"fight","won":true}},{"t":"say","text":"Before the dark takes him he stops, lifts a shuttered lamp, and opens it twice, toward the shaft.\n\nThe hill knows you are still out here. Whatever is being made ready down there will not wait for you."},{"t":"say","text":"He fought without a word. And then he ran."},{"t":"say","text":"Where he stood to make his signal, the turf is worn through to an old cut stone, with a hollow in it the size of a hand."},{"t":"act","label":"REACH IN"},{"t":"say","text":"Cold, under the dew. The lip of the hollow is worn smooth, by hands, over a very long time.\n\n**A locked Seeker Fragment has been added to your Chest.**","fragment":true},{"t":"say","text":"**There is no second door on this hillside, and now there is a clock. Last week, six cold slivers showed you a way nobody was watching. You have five.**","pull":true},{"t":"summary","lines":["**THE HILLSIDE** · Day 5","You earned: `[gold]`","You learned: they wear **a small black circle**. One of them fought you without a word, ran, and signalled the hill. Meira could not find his name anywhere: *someone wanted him forgotten.*","You hold: **the black circle** · the horn button, matched to his cuff","Fragments: 5 found","Tomorrow: **the lip of the shaft**"]}]}$json$::jsonb, $json${"dc":7,"wDef":23,"wAtk":16,"fightReward":300}$json$::jsonb),
('dark-moon', 1, 2, 6, $json${"week":2,"day":6,"title":"The other way in","heading":"The lip of the shaft","question":"is there another way in, and how long is left?","steps":[{"t":"say","text":"Your second night on the hill. Two lamps burn at the foot of the shaft, and the ladder has not come back.\n\nIt is your watch. You lie on your belly at the lip, with the cold coming up out of the ground into your elbows."},{"t":"notice","lines":{"Might":{"first":"Under your palm the ground is trembling, very slightly.","second":"It is not the river."},"Agility":{"first":"The two at the foot of the shaft change places every little while.","second":"They are tired. They have been at this for days."},"Intellect":{"first":"They have not come up after you, and they have not put their lamps out.","second":"They are not afraid of you. They are only keeping you where you are."},"Charm":{"first":"The chanting has started again.","second":"Whatever they were making ready is nearly ready."},"Craft":{"first":"A sound comes up the shaft, and then the same sound comes up through the ground, a moment later.","second":"There is more hollow under this hill than one room."},"Aim":{"first":"The lamplight at the bottom dims and brightens.","second":"People are crossing in front of it, and all of them the same way."}}},{"t":"challenge","title":"READ THE HILL","desc":"You cannot see them. You can hear them, and you can watch their light.","options":[{"attr":"Aim","verb":"count the shapes crossing the lamp, and place them"},{"attr":"Might","verb":"haul yourself up to the crack above the lamp, and look down into it"}],"reward":"+500g","fail":"you know only that there are many, and that they are busy"},{"t":"say","text":"Shape by shape, you place them as they cross the light. You have them: a knot of them at the lamps, a steady file beyond, all going the same way. And one who does not move at all, and is small.","cond":{"on":"challenge","pass":true}},{"t":"say","text":"You watch until your eyes ache from the lamplight and the shapes run together. There are many. They are busy. That is all the hill will tell you.","cond":{"on":"challenge","pass":false}},{"t":"press","title":"EAR TO THE ROCK","detail":"listen below the room you can place","harder":4,"reward":"+200g, and one more detail"},{"t":"say","text":"You lay your ear to the cold rock and wait for the chant to come round again. Above, it is muffled and close. Below it there is something else: a silence with room in it.\n\nUnder the room with the lamps there is another hollow. It is bigger. And there is nobody in it at all.","cond":{"on":"press"}},{"t":"say","text":"Somewhere in the long hours it turns up: not hidden, this time. Lying among the roots at the lip of the shaft, as if it had been dropped there yesterday."},{"t":"act","label":"PICK IT UP"},{"t":"say","text":"**A locked Seeker Fragment has been added to your Chest.**\n\nThat is six.","fragment":true},{"t":"act","label":"LAY THEM OUT"},{"t":"say","text":"They move, as the first six did. Each turns a little, and settles against the next. And then they are one thing.\n\nA map, old and exact. It points into this same hill. Not to the chamber that drove you back, but deeper: to an older room, reached by a shaft of its own, cut long before any of those hooded figures was born."},{"t":"say","text":"The others are strung out along the hillside on watch, too far apart to pass a map between. They have to have it too."},{"t":"choice","id":0,"labels":["READ IT OUT","LET {F3} READ IT"],"mode":"flavor","branches":[]},{"t":"say","text":"It is said aloud, twice, across the dark, so that everybody has it.\n\nThe night is very still. Sound carries."},{"t":"say","text":"The map marks a place two hundred paces along the hill."},{"t":"act","label":"GO AND PUT YOUR HAND TO IT"},{"t":"say","text":"A fall of old stone, grown over. Under it, when you have shifted enough of it: a hole. Cold air is breathing out of it.\n\nIt is real. And nobody is guarding it."},{"t":"say","text":"Within the hour, the hill wakes.\n\nLamps. Feet. A child's voice, cut short. All of it moving deeper.\n\nAnd then, far down in the rock: picks."},{"t":"say","text":"Even here, Garrick pours one more cup than there are of you, and sets it on a flat stone at the empty place. There is not much left in the flask. He pours it anyway."},{"t":"say","text":"**They are digging toward the old room. Be in it first.**","pull":true},{"t":"summary","lines":["**THE OTHER WAY IN** · Day 6","You earned: `[gold]` · Aim or Might `[growth]`","You learned: **the six fragments are a map again.** It shows an older room, deeper in the same hill, with a shaft of its own. You found its mouth. Nobody is guarding it. They are digging toward that room now.","*On a failure:* You missed something on the hill. Someone at the fire may have seen it.","You hold: the map · the black circle","Fragments: 6 of 6 · the map is whole","Tomorrow: **THE GATHERING** · into the hill by the old shaft, together"]}]}$json$::jsonb, $json${"dc":7,"wDef":23,"wAtk":16,"fightReward":0}$json$::jsonb)
